  "reason": "R13 and R15 establish that moment tensor potentials can provide an accurate, computationally efficient representation of a closely related BCC refractory multicomponent alloy, while R5 and R11 show that interatomic-potential simulations can capture chemically meaningful short-range order in refractory HEAs. R1, R2, R19, and R20 more generally show that small electronic, magnetic, or entropic free-energy contributions can shift phase stability. However, none of the records proposes using an MTP specifically for liquid-phase sampling, replacing thermodynamic integration with MTP-to-DFT free-energy perturbation, exploiting the low variance of MTP–DFT energy differences, or incorporating a Fermi-level DOS gap and SRO stabilization into melting-point calculations. Thus, the records point toward accurate ML potentials and relevant free-energy corrections, but the combined MTP/FEP melting workflow would still require a substantial new idea."
